(Photosynthesis and Cellular Respiration - Study Notes) Tj T*
(Biology 101, Week 4. Key definitions, formulas and processes.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(1. Core Definitions) Tj T*
(Photosynthesis: the process by which green plants, algae and some) Tj T*
(bacteria convert light energy into chemical energy stored in glucose.) Tj T*
(Chlorophyll: the green pigment in chloroplasts that absorbs light,) Tj T*
(mainly in the blue and red wavelengths; reflects green.) Tj T*
(Stomata: pores on the leaf underside that regulate gas exchange.) Tj T*
(ATP \(adenosine triphosphate\): the cell's main energy currency.) Tj T*
(NADPH: electron carrier produced in the light reactions.) Tj T*
(Calvin cycle: the light-independent reactions that fix CO2 into sugar.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(2. The Master Equation) Tj T*
(6 CO2 + 6 H2O + light energy -> C6H12O6 + 6 O2) Tj T*
(Carbon dioxide + water, powered by light, yield glucose and oxygen.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(3. Two Stages of Photosynthesis) Tj T*
(Stage A - Light reactions \(thylakoid membranes\):) Tj T*
(  - Light splits water \(photolysis\), releasing O2.) Tj T*
(  - Electron transport chain builds ATP and NADPH.) Tj T*
(Stage B - Calvin cycle \(stroma\):) Tj T*
(  - Carbon fixation: RuBisCO attaches CO2 to RuBP.) Tj T*
(  - Reduction: ATP and NADPH convert 3-PGA into G3P.) Tj T*
(  - Regeneration: RuBP is rebuilt so the cycle can continue.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(4. Cellular Respiration - the mirror process) Tj T*
(C6H12O6 + 6 O2 -> 6 CO2 + 6 H2O + ATP \(about 30-32 ATP per glucose\)) Tj T*
(Glycolysis \(cytoplasm\) -> Krebs cycle \(mitochondrial matrix\) ->) Tj T*
(oxidative phosphorylation \(inner mitochondrial membrane\).) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(5. Frequently Confused Pairs) Tj T*
(Chlorophyll vs chloroplast: pigment vs organelle.) Tj T*
(Light reactions vs Calvin cycle: energy capture vs carbon fixation.) Tj T*
(Aerobic vs anaerobic respiration: with vs without oxygen.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(6. Practice Questions) Tj T*
(Q1. Where exactly does the Calvin cycle take place?) Tj T*
(Q2. Which molecule is both a reactant of respiration and a product) Tj T*
(of photosynthesis? \(Hint: there are two correct answers.\)) Tj T*
(Q3. Explain why the light reactions stop within seconds in the dark) Tj T*
(while the Calvin cycle can continue briefly.) Tj T*
ET
